 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? A lot more than you'd think. Most people learn the plot and vocabulary first, so they' not lost on the actual language. You don't need them. Try it without, and see what you can piece together. One or two is fine, more only adds stress. Try to watch a show you' already seen in English, it's a lot easier than something new. Enjoyable and familiar is good. You could even watch with the subtitles off for bit if you get bored.",
